xact Gauss sums) is proved; the\nlinear regime is \\\\cref{lem:vanish}; only this exceptional-channel\nbookkeeping remains.\n\\\\end{openproblem}\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen('finite_spectral_shadows.tex','w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode finite_spectral_shadows.tex >/tmp/fss.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode finite_spectral_shadows.tex >/tmp/fss.log 2>&1\ngrep -E \"^!\" /tmp/fss.log | head -3; pdfinfo finite_spectral_shadows.pdf | grep Pages","input_hash":"sha256:99b7c566a12bd06ead2d5ad5acfebddfddd170ad1f43a261f4e49086ff66bdb8","output_hash":"sha256:b6477796b7d4514543b77d0038404c133fb17e4896f318876441e851d39327bf","tool":"Bash"},"time":"2026-06-10T07:53:02Z"},{"actor":{"kind":"ai_tool","tool":"Claude Code"},"event_type":"command_run","materiality_hint":{"possible_code_effect":true},"target":{"command":"cd /home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory\nailog add --tool claude-code --level-hint 2 --text \"dc_28 cellwise summation: QUADRATIC ROUTE PROVED, exceptional channels isolated (36pp). (1) FACTORIZATION: L'(a) = -sum_i term_i(L)(a)*g_i(a), g_i = 3^i(2*3^i a+C_i+C'_i)u_i(a) - each second-derivative term = first-derivative term x extra factor of valuation i+v3(sumfactor). (2) LEMMA (lem:quadval, quadratic valuation/unique minimum): v3(L'(a)) = d+i_min EXACTLY for class-IV pairs - the 3^i-GRADING makes active L'-term valuations d+i STRICTLY INCREASING => unique minimum => cancellation (the mechanism that created the degeneracy in L) is IMPOSSIBLE in L'; sumfactor = 2C_i mod 3 unit automatically when v3(dC_i)>=1. Two explicit exception channels: (E1) sumfactor exception C+C' = 0 mod 3 (only at unit-level actives), (E2) inactive tie at i_min-1 with v=d+1 + digit cancellation. AUDIT c=7: 300/300 class-IV points have v3(L') = d+i_min, ZERO exceptions. Same one-level-deeper grading mechanism as the F-bijectivity lemma of op:flat. (3) Exact quadratic Gauss: |sum e(Bt^2+At)/3^l| in {0, 3^{l/2}} 